<h2>Winter Strategies (December-February)</h2>
<p>Winter is the make-or-break season for heating contractors. Emergency furnace repair calls peak, replacement demand surges after failures, and the contractors who prepared in fall reap the rewards. But winter isn&#39;t just about emergency response — it&#39;s also an opportunity to market indoor air quality and position your company for the year ahead.</p>
<h3>Strategy 10: Run Emergency Heating Repair PPC</h3>
<p><strong>The Strategy:</strong></p>
<p>Winter emergency heating PPC follows the same playbook as summer AC emergency campaigns, with one critical difference: the stakes are higher. A family without heat in January faces genuine health risks, not just discomfort. This urgency means higher close rates, higher average tickets, and stronger customer loyalty — if you respond fast.</p>
<p><strong>How to Execute:</strong></p>
<p>Emergency heating keywords command similar CPCs to summer AC terms — <strong>$15-$40+</strong> depending on market and competition. But winter conversion rates are often higher because the need is more acute. A homeowner can survive a night without AC. A night without heat in Minnesota is a different story.</p>
<p><strong>Keyword Strategy:</strong></p>
