<li><strong>Facebook/Instagram:</strong> Run video ads showing heat pump installations and customer testimonials. Target homeowners 40-65, environmentally conscious audiences, and recent home buyers.</li>
<li><strong>Email to existing customers:</strong> &quot;Is 2025 the Year You Go Electric?&quot; — pitch heat pumps to customers with aging systems who are due for replacement anyway.</li>
<li><strong>Partnerships:</strong> Partner with local solar installers, electricians, and energy auditors. They encounter customers interested in electrification and can refer heat pump prospects to you.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>The Sales Consultation:</strong></p>
<p>Heat pump sales require a longer consultation than standard replacements. Homeowners need education, not just a quote. Structure your sales process as a consultation:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Assessment:</strong> Evaluate the home&#39;s insulation, ductwork, and electrical panel capacity</li>
<li><strong>Education:</strong> Explain how heat pumps work, show performance data for your climate, and walk through the incentive stack</li>
<li><strong>Options:</strong> Present 2-3 system options with different efficiency levels and price points</li>
<li><strong>Financing:</strong> Offer payment plans that make the monthly cost comparable to current utility bills</li>
<li><strong>Timeline:</strong> Set clear expectations for installation timing, especially if targeting the federal tax credit deadline</li>
